def features():
    out=['Statuses are exclusive for the feature scope named. IMPLEMENTED is source-traceable and bounded by the documented local acceptance; it does not mean production-ready. Evidence upload is partial relative to broad document-format/scanning requirements, even though its narrow text workflow exists.','', '| Feature | Status | Sprint | Backend | Frontend | Database | Tests | Evidence |','|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
    for name,status,sprint,back,front,db,mig,tests,api in FEATURES:
        out.append(f'| {name} | {status} | {sprint} | `{back}` | `{front}` | `{db}` | `{tests}` | detail below / creating migration `{mig}` |')
    for name,status,sprint,back,front,db,mig,tests,api in FEATURES:
        out += [f'## Evidence: {name}','',f'- **Status:** {status}',f'- **Implementation file:** `{back.split(":")[0]}` (API paths resolve under `services/api/ppm_api` unless explicit).',f'- **Important class/function:** `{back}`',f'- **Database table:** `{db}`',f'- **API endpoint:** `{api}`',f'- **Frontend component:** `{front}` (web paths resolve under `apps/web` unless explicit).',f'- **Migration:** `{mig}` under `services/api/migrations/versions` where applicable.',f'- **Tests:** `{tests}`',f'- **Verification:** '+('Current source traced; prior local acceptance is linked from the corresponding sprint report. No new integration execution claimed by this row.' if status in ['IMPLEMENTED','PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED'] else 'Not confirmed as runtime functionality from the current workspace.'),'']
        if status=='PLANNED': out+=['**Planned — not verified as implemented in the current workspace.**','']
    out+=['## Evidence interpretation','','Specific entities are expanded in the [database dictionary](DATABASE-DICTIONARY.md), public operations in [API inventory](18-api-contracts.md), and source/test symbols in [code index](CODE-AND-TEST-INDEX.md). These references cover subordinate resources without inventing a separate frontend component for every SQL table. Individual ownership is not established by feature presence.']
    write('26-feature-status.md','Feature status and evidence register','\n'.join(out))

QA=[
('Explain the actual backend request chain.','`RecordEditor.save` → shared transport → Next proxy → `main.request_context` → FastAPI parsing/`principal` → `delivery.write` → Core/asyncpg → PostgreSQL → `view`/RecordView → React reload. It is not a JPA repository chain.','delivery.py'),
('Why FastAPI in this project?','It supplies typed route/dependency/response contracts that drive the generated web client. `create_app` centralizes lifecycle, routers and safe errors. A historical comparison against every other framework is not recorded.','main.py'),
('Why PostgreSQL?','The implementation relies on transactions, RLS, tenant/project composite foreign keys, numeric money and JSONB snapshots. These are concrete code dependencies, not a generic popularity claim.','../migrations/versions/0003_delivery.py'),
('Why SQLAlchemy?','Core expressions, async pooling and shared metadata connect typed domain logic to bound SQL and migrations. Domain writes use explicit AsyncConnection operations.','database.py'),
('Why Alembic?','Six ordered frozen revisions evolve an existing database independently from Python model edits, with separate owner credentials and guarded test lifecycle.','../migrations/env.py'),
('Is there an ORM Session?','Not in the inspected domain request path. `principal` yields an AsyncConnection and code consumes row mappings. FoundationState is declarative, but that does not establish a Session identity map.','identity.py'),
('How is startup handled?','Lifespan validates Settings and creates engine/Redis/storage, then disposes/closes on shutdown. Migrations run in a separate Compose service; readiness checks the expected head.','main.py'),
('Where does authentication happen?','`Auth` resolves `principal`: JWT verification, live session, membership, verified user and CSRF binding before yielding the principal.','identity.py'),
('What is inside the access token?','sub, sid, org, iat, exp, issuer enterprise-ppm, audience ppm-web and jti; signed HS256 with ten-minute expiry. Role is read live instead of accepted from a stale token.','identity.py'),
('Why keep a DB session with JWT?','Immediate revocation, fixed seven-day lifetime, active organization and CSRF binding must be checked on every protected request. Signature validity alone cannot prove present authorization.','identity.py'),
('How are passwords handled?','bcrypt cost 12, new minimum 12 characters and maximum 72 UTF-8 bytes, thread-offloaded hashing/checking and dummy hash for absent identity.','identity.py'),
('How does refresh replay behave?','Session row locking serializes rotation. A used digest causes session revocation; code commits it before returning 401. In-page transport coalesces refresh, while independent tabs can still race.','identity.py'),
('Where are browser tokens stored?','Secure HttpOnly Strict cookies for access/refresh; readable CSRF cookie for request header. Not localStorage. The Next proxy forwards Set-Cookie.','identity.py'),
('How is CSRF prevented?','Unsafe methods require exact Origin and matching CSRF cookie/header. Authenticated unsafe requests also compare the header digest to the session CSRF hash.','main.py'),
('Can anyone register an organization Admin?','No public self-registration route does that. Operator bootstrap creates initial organization/pending Admin; challenge completion activates or accepts controlled invitations.','identity.py'),
('Authentication versus authorization?','principal identifies a live caller; authorize/can_edit/reviewer decide permitted operations. Admin organization role does not make the actor the assigned assessment respondent.','delivery.py'),
('Where does tenant identity come from?','Signed claim verified against live session and active membership. X-Organization-ID is only a stale-tab precondition and cannot elevate authority.','identity.py'),
('How does RLS get the tenant?','`context` sets user/org/role via parameter-bound set_config with transaction-local true. Policies read current_setting and reject unmatched tenant rows.','identity.py'),
('Can database owners bypass RLS?','The design relies on a separate non-owner NOBYPASSRLS app role. It does not claim universal FORCE RLS or owner-proof immutability.','../migrations/versions/0003_delivery.py'),
('Why composite foreign keys?','Including tenant and sometimes project IDs prevents a valid foreign UUID from connecting records across organizations or attaching work to a foreign project sprint.','ppm_tables.py'),
('How does a PM create a project?','Needs a portfolio manage grant, valid organization setup and references; the atomic write adds the project and a creator manage grant alongside audit/receipt.','delivery.py'),
('Where is input validated?','FastAPI/Pydantic validates shape/types/ranges; write/refs validate business state/scope; PostgreSQL enforces constraints/RLS at execution.','ppm_schemas.py'),
('Why not expose table rows directly?','Internal creator/snapshot fields and server-owned scope differ from API payload. `view` and RecordView make the public contract explicit and validate response data.','delivery.py'),
('How is SQL generated?','A Core select/insert/update expression compiles through PostgreSQL dialect, passes bound parameters to asyncpg and executes on the checked-out connection. Result mappings are then serialized.','database.py'),
('When does a write commit?','Execute sends SQL within the transaction; `engine.begin` context completion commits. A later domain exception rolls back project/audit/receipt together.','identity.py'),
('What does rollback fail to undo?','A filesystem object already written is outside PostgreSQL atomicity; assessment upload may leave orphan bytes if metadata transaction fails.','assessment.py'),
('What happens with two concurrent project edits?','Both send revision N; organization lock serializes them. First writes N+1; second rechecks and fails 412, with final SQL revision predicate as another guard.','delivery.py'),
('Why an organization advisory lock?','It coordinates membership authority and cross-record invariants plus snapshot consistency. It is intentionally coarse and can limit throughput.','delivery.py'),
('How do retries avoid duplicate creates?','UUID idempotency receipt scoped to org/user plus canonical payload/resource fingerprint. Conflicting reuse 409; identical replay rechecks authority and retrieves current target.','delivery.py'),
('Is assessment idempotency identical?','No. Its mutation fingerprint includes method/path/raw bytes/If-Match, and stored response is replayed after live command access checks.','assessment.py'),
('How are baseline plans preserved?','New baseline version freezes current project and selected child facts into JSONB and app-role update/delete is absent. Later plans append rather than mutate history.','delivery.py'),
('How are financial mistakes corrected?','Append a same-project/currency exact negative reversal of the original; unique reversal reference and validation prevent duplicate or reversal-of-reversal corrections.','delivery.py'),
('How does budget utilization handle incomplete data?','`budget_usage` returns null when approved budget is zero or ledger incomplete; otherwise Decimal spend×100/budget. Currency groups stay separate.','metric_math.py'),
('How is strategic alignment computed?','Only active goal contributions whose weights total exactly 1 qualify: Σweight×contribution×100. Missing/incomplete weights produce null.','metric_math.py'),
('How are dependency cycles stopped?','Node and project graphs undergo topological traversal. Cross-project changes require Admin so hidden edges cannot invalidate the check.','delivery.py'),
('Is a resource the same as a user?','No. A resource is a workforce profile; login/membership authority remains identity data. Resource manage/effort permissions are explicit.','capacity.py'),
('How do capacity dates work?','Local dates [start,end), effective immutable calendar weekday hours minus holiday/leave; DST does not alter declared scheduled hours.','capacity.py'),
('What happens to allocations on leave?','They remain counted on scheduled weekdays, exposing over-allocation against reduced availability. Missing calendar leaves capacity unknown.','capacity.py'),
('Why sum daily excess instead of total differences?','Spare capacity on another day cannot cancel overload on a specific date. `calculate` clamps each day then summary sums daily excess.','capacity.py'),
('When is actual utilization valid?','Sensitive effort grant, full resource scope, complete daily attestations and nonzero known availability. Effort edits invalidate coverage.','capacity.py'),
('Can Admin read all sensitive effort by default?','No, separate effort capability is required even for Admin. PM project slices cannot claim whole-resource overload.','capacity.py'),
('How are small teams protected?','Team summary requires Admin and at least five members on every selected date; otherwise suppressed/insufficient scope. No medical prediction is made.','capacity.py'),
('How is an assessment definition versioned?','Editable framework JSONB publishes immutable version snapshots; assignment references that version and answers validate against its question IDs.','assessment.py'),
('Explain the scoring algorithm.','Boolean→0/1; rubric→(v−min)/(max−min); dimension=100×weighted numeric sum/answered numeric weight; overall weighted by dimensions totaling 1; unknown dimension makes overall null.','assessment.py'),
('What do text answers do?','They affect required completeness and answer coverage but do not enter numeric score denominator/numerator. No semantic AI evaluates them.','assessment.py'),
('Score versus evidence coverage?','Score measures rubric values; weighted answer coverage measures valid answers; evidence coverage counts questions with narrative or released attachment. Neither evidence presence nor score proves truth.','assessment.py'),
('Can a reviewer alter raw answers?','Review stores a reasoned numeric override separately, validates target and independent assignment, and logs adjustment history. Respondent edits later clear reviewer adjustments.','assessment.py'),
('How are evidence attachments protected?','Narrow base64 UTF-8 text bounds, generated tenant paths, SHA256, quarantine and independent release, live access/digest checks on download. It is not antivirus.','assessment.py'),
('How does dashboard health work?','Schedule/financial/capacity risk components are bounded 0–100; risk=.4s+.35f+.25c; health=100−risk. Missing any component makes unknown; policy maps risk to Red/Amber/Green.','command.py'),
('Can Green have a discrepancy while computed health is unknown?','Yes. A reported Green project with overdue open critical milestone is flagged independently of the full composite risk.','command.py'),
('Is risk a probability?','No. Fixed weighted deterministic risk points have no trained probability/calibration interpretation.','command.py'),
('How is velocity kept stable?','Sprint close freezes completed points and source work into sprint_closures. Missing/incomplete old closures stay unknown; later task edits do not rewrite past velocity.','delivery.py'),
('What is source freshness?','Age of the oldest contributing updated_at compared with policy stale_days, distinct from the time snapshot was recomputed. Reload cannot renew source evidence.','command.py'),
('Does a date filter reconstruct historical health?','No. It filters period spend/benefits/closed sprints/capacity while health/budget are labelled current state.','command.py'),
('What if Redis fails?','Shared identity limit operations fail closed and readiness fails. It also disrupts checkpoint broker/results; it is not a cached authority for project rows.','identity.py'),
('What if the worker crashes?','Only the checkpoint task is implemented; no durable business-job reconciliation can be claimed. Outbox/leases/retries are Sprint 08 plans.','../../worker/ppm_worker/app.py'),
('What AI is actually implemented?','No provider/RAG/embedding/agent/model-serving path verified. Current assessment and command metrics are deterministic, with planned AI specified separately.','assessment.py'),
('Why would you add RAG or an agent?','As proposed future work, retrieval could supply scoped evidence and typed read tools could support reviewable suggestions. No current RAG/agent benefit is claimed as delivered.','command.py'),
('How would you scale it?','Measure query/pool/lock cost, batch repeated source reads, preserve scope/unknown semantics, then implement durable projections/jobs and narrower coordination where justified. These are proposals.','command.py'),
('What does CI prove?','Workflow defines static/contracts/unit/real-stack/browser/persistence checks. Recorded acceptance is local; no hosted CI or deployment result is verified.','main.py'),
('How would you add a module?','Use strict schemas, domain helpers, Auth/lock/scoped Core queries, new frozen migration with policies/privileges, generated contracts, UI and negative security/concurrency tests.','delivery.py'),
('What is the role of frontend TypeScript?','Generated types improve compile-time agreement; React local state renders responses. Type assertions in local fetch wrappers do not runtime-validate arbitrary JSON.','ppm_schemas.py'),
('What did you personally build?','Use Backend Engineering as role. Feature presence and two savepoint commits do not prove individual authorship of all frontend, AI or infrastructure. Say ownership not verified where appropriate.','main.py')
]

def interview():
    out=['These scripts describe project behavior. Use first-person contribution claims only when you can substantiate your own work. Default role: **Backend Engineering**.','', '## 30-second explanation','','“AI-PPM through Sprint 07 is a local enterprise PPM application with a FastAPI backend, PostgreSQL system of record and Next.js frontend. It supports tenant-scoped project delivery, capacity planning, versioned assessments and four dashboards. Its backend emphasizes live authorization, database row policies, atomic audit history and concurrency checks. Current scores are deterministic; AI integration remains planned.”','', '## 2-minute explanation','','“The business goal is to connect portfolio decisions to reliable delivery facts. A React form sends a typed request through a same-origin Next proxy. FastAPI validates the contract, resolves a JWT against a live session and membership, and establishes transaction-local tenant context. Domain functions authorize the action and use SQLAlchemy Core connections to write PostgreSQL. RLS and composite foreign keys reinforce application checks. Project writes, audit and retry receipts share a transaction, while revision checks reject stale edits.\n\nResource planning combines immutable calendars, leave and allocations without claiming utilization from hidden or incomplete data. Assessment scores use frozen published rubrics and independent review, not an LLM. Command-center health derives from schedule, financial and capacity evidence, preserves unknown inputs and flags optimistic human reports. The local stack includes Redis and a Celery checkpoint worker, but durable business jobs, RAG and agents are later roadmap work. Recorded verification is local, not a production certification.”','', '## 5-minute technical explanation','','Spend roughly one minute on the business/fact model, then trace project create for two minutes: RecordEditor, transport/CSRF, fixed proxy, middleware, principal, organization lock, live authority, ProjectInput, refs, INSERT RETURNING, audit and receipt, response/UI reload. Spend one minute on failure semantics: stale revision 412, key conflict 409, hidden ID 404, rollback and immutable reversal. Finish with one worked metric and the honest AI/deployment boundary. Use chapter 04 as the exact spoken trace; show delivery.write and command.combined as the two code anchors.','', '## 15-minute deep technical explanation','','Use this timed route through real source, explaining the why and one failure at each stage.','', '| Time | Explanation and demonstration |','|---|---|','| 0–2 min | Problem and current architecture; distinguish Sprint 07 implementation from roadmap |','| 2–5 min | Create-project trace; show Auth dependency, Core connection and response envelope |','| 5–7 min | JWT/live session, tenant context, app-role RLS and composite FK |','| 7–9 min | Two revision-N writers, idempotency replay and record/audit/receipt atomicity |','| 9–11 min | Capacity daily excess or assessment weighted score; derive one numeric example |','| 11–13 min | Dashboard all-input requirement, provenance, frozen velocity and discrepancy |','| 13–14 min | Real tests/CI boundaries and worker checkpoint limitations |','| 14–15 min | Coarse-lock/query tradeoffs; measured future scaling and planned AI |','', 'The timing guides depth; it is not a claim that a short paragraph takes fifteen minutes to read. Use the full explanations and code walks in the linked chapters, not unsupported memorized claims.','', f'## {len(QA)} code-grounded interview questions and answers','']
    for i,(q,a,file) in enumerate(QA,1):
        path=(ROOT/'services/api/ppm_api'/file).resolve().relative_to(ROOT).as_posix()
        out += [f'### {i}. {q}','',a+f' Evidence: [{path}](../{path}).','']
    body='\n'.join(out)
    before=body.split('## 5-minute technical explanation')[0]
    questions=body[body.index(f'## {len(QA)} code-grounded interview questions and answers'):]
    body=before+'## 5-minute technical explanation\n\n'+FIVE_MINUTES+'\n\n## 15-minute deep technical explanation\n\n'+FIFTEEN_MINUTES+'\n\n'+questions
    write('29-interview-preparation.md','Interview preparation',body)

